udio 1>: partially_copy - all dialogue, voices, pauses, emotional delivery, and timing from <Audio 1> are copied exactly, while natural rain ambience is generated separately.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses intimate live-action cinematic realism, natural overcast lighting, muted rural colors, shallow depth of field, visible rainfall, and restrained handheld movement. Both characters are completely soaked. Rainwater runs continuously over their hair, faces, hands, and clothing. The uploaded <Audio 1> controls the exact lip movements, speaker changes, pauses, and dialogue timing.\n\n[Shot 1] Following <Picture 2>, <Subject 2> stands with her back to the camera while holding <Subject 1>'s face between both hands. His wet face is framed tightly between her fingers. His eyes are red and glossy, his brows tremble, and he struggles to maintain eye contact. From 00:00.000 to 00:01.700, <Subject 1> (S1) synchronizes precisely with the male voice in <Audio 1> and says: <d>[Chinese] 你为什么还要来找我……</d> His mouth shapes, jaw movement, trembling lower lip, and final exhale follow the audio exactly. <Subject 2> listens with her lips completely closed.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.820, the camera cuts to the reverse composition of <Picture 1>. <Subject 2>'s rain-covered face appears beyond <Subject 1>'s blurred head and shoulder. Her hands never release him. From 00:01.940 to 00:04.540, <Subject 2> (S2) synchronizes precisely with the female voice in <Audio 1> and says: <d>[Chinese] 你以为躲起来，我就找不到你了吗？</d> Her right thumb gently brushes rainwater from his cheek. <Subject 1> keeps his lips completely closed and reacts only through his eyes and breathing.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.700, the camera cuts back to the composition of <Picture 2>. <Subject 1>'s breathing becomes uneven. His gaze drops briefly in shame before returning to her eyes. From 00:04.860 to 00:06.440, <Subject 1> (S1) synchronizes with the returning male voice and says: <d>[Chinese] 我已经不是以前那个我了……</d> He closes his mout